      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Ventura sits on land once part of a 40‑mile Neutral Ground created by the 1825 Treaty of Prairie du Chien, letting Sioux, Sauk, and Meskwaki hunt peacefully.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/ventura_iowa",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Chicago, Milwaukee and St. Paul Railroad finished its line from Algona to Clear Lake on August 3, 1877, bringing Ventura into the national rail network.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10,
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/ventura_iowa",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1852, a Meskwaki band led by Chief Ko‑ko‑wa passed Ventura en route to a final intertribal clash with Sioux near the East Des Moines River.",
